    the Kotlin parameter default ONLY for a body param, whose value the SDK
    serializes and sends — there the default is the value the caller gets when
    they omit the argument, mirroring how model properties carry their default.
    A query/header/form/cookie param is the opposite: its default is applied
    server-side, and the omit-on-unset contract (an absent optional param must
    send NO key at all, see the allowEmptyValue tests) requires it stay null so
    nothing is materialised onto the wire. `defaultValue` is the codegen literal;
    a string body default is the bare token and must be quoted to form a valid
    String literal, while numeric/boolean/enum-reference defaults are already
    valid Kotlin expressions and are emitted verbatim. }}
